Subject: RICH: Video magazines

I think one serious disadvantage of video magazines is that there's no
way to "flip" through them conveniently.  The human eye is remarkably
good at extracting a sought-after item from a massive visual barrage,
so one can flip the pages of a magazine and extract interesting
information very efficiently.  Fast-forward on a VCR would be much
less efficient, I think.

Also, most of the added benefits of a video magazine seem to fall
under emotional and sensory stimulation, rather than information
content per se.  Stimulation is pretty well supplied by the current
entertainment media.

